  "instance_name": "anchor_baby_rhetoric",
  "label": "Anti-Immigrant Stereotype",
  "description": "The term 'anchor baby' refers to a child born to undocumented immigrants in the U.S., which is often used in anti-immigrant rhetoric to suggest that such children grant citizenship to their parents, thereby 'anchoring' them in the country. This stereotype is used in the meme to imply that granting rights to immigrants is unfair to those who 'do have rights,' which is a misleading and inflammatory claim.",
